FAQ = [
 ("What is the best LED light kit for a Jeep Wrangler JL?",
  "For most owners, the Baja Designs LP6 Pro bumper kit. It bolts two LP6 Pro lights to the factory bumper mounting points with OEM-style brackets, includes the wiring harness, and carries a limited lifetime warranty. RealTruck lists it at $1,159.95 with 11,225 lumens of primary output. Bumper lights sit much lower than a windshield bar, which cuts glare off the hood and keeps them closer to the mounting heights most states allow. Buy the version for your bumper: Baja sells separate steel and plastic bumper kits."),
 ("Are LED light bars legal on a Jeep Wrangler?",
  "Usually only off-road. Rules vary by state, but CJ Pony Parts' state summary quotes California requiring off-road lights to be off and covered with an opaque cover, Pennsylvania requiring them off and covered on public roads, and North Carolina requiring light bars off while driving on public roads. Many states also cap the number of auxiliary lamps at two or three and set mounting heights. A 50 in windshield bar is an off-road light. Check your state's code before you drive with one uncovered."),
 ("Do I need a cover for my JL light bar?",
  "In several states, yes. CJ Pony Parts cites California's rule that off-road lights be off and covered with an opaque cover on the highway, and KC HiLiTES notes Pennsylvania requires covers on roof-mounted off-road lights. The KC Gravity Pro6 50 in kit ships with eight protective covers, one per light. Covers also protect lenses from branches and rocks, so they are worth keeping on when you aren't using the lights."),
 ("Will a JL windshield light bar kit fit the 4xe or Rubicon 392?",
  "Not always. Quadratec's page for the KC 91336 50 in kit excludes 4xe hybrid models, and ExtremeTerrain's page excludes the Rubicon 392. KC sells separate 50 in overhead bracket sets for the 392/Mojave (7328) and the 4xe (7331). Hawkley's A-pillar brackets are listed as not for 4xe or Mojave. Baja Designs says the Mojave and 392 cowl is taller and needs longer M6 x 80 mm bolts for its A-pillar kit."),
 ("How do I wire an LED light bar on a JL?",
  "Buy a kit with a harness. The KC 50 in kit includes a wiring harness with a switch, and Baja offers its bumper and A-pillar kits with either a toggle-switch harness or an upfitter harness. The upfitter version is meant to connect to a factory auxiliary switch system if your JL has one. A proper harness includes a relay and a fuse sized for the light's current draw; don't splice a bar directly into a headlight circuit."),
 ("How many watts or lumens do I need?",
  "It depends on where the light points. The KC Gravity Pro6 50 in bar is 160 watts and 18,400 raw lumens, with a claimed 1,637 m beam distance, which suits open desert and fire roads. Baja's Squadron Sport A-pillar pods are 3,200 lumens and 30 watts each, meant to light the trail edges and corners. For tight wooded trails, wide cornering beams near the front do more good than a long-range bar on the roof."),
 ("Does a windshield light bar cause glare or noise on a JL?",
  "None of the maker pages we read give glare or noise figures. A roof-line bar sits above and behind the hood, so some of its light can reflect off the hood toward the driver, while bumper and A-pillar lights sit ahead of or beside it. The makers don't make claims about wind noise either way. If you drive long highway stretches and want to avoid the question, a bumper kit keeps the lights out of the airflow over the windshield."),
 ("Do light bar brackets require drilling on the JL?",
  "The better kits use factory mounting points. Baja says its A-pillar kit mounts at factory locations with no trimming, and RealTruck describes the LP6 Pro bumper kit as OEM-style brackets mounting to factory locations. Windshield brackets such as Nilight's and Hawkley's bolt to the windshield frame and A-pillar. Read the install sheet for any budget bracket before you buy."),
 ("Do 2018–2023 light bar brackets fit the 2024 facelifted JL?",
  "Often, but check the listing. The 2024 update brought a new grille and interior, per Wikipedia, and bracket listings end in different years: the Nilight windshield bracket lists 2018–2023, Hawkley's lists 2018–2026, and Auto Dynasty's older brackets stop at 2020. Grille-mounted lights are the most likely to change with the new grille. Buy the listing that names your model year."),
 ("Should I buy a cheap light bar or a brand-name one?",
  "The difference is mostly in optics, sealing and warranty. Baja backs its lights with a limited lifetime warranty and replaceable optics, and KC's Gravity Pro6 is rated IP68. Budget bars often don't publish a lumen figure you can compare or a sealing standard. A cheap bracket paired with a mid-priced bar is a reasonable compromise, as long as the bracket's listing names your JL and model year."),
]

